  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "while \"ながら\" is a word used in speaking, ”つつ\" is used in writing. if you know some other similar situations regarding other words listed on JGram, please post this kind of explanation, won't you.",
      "html": "while \"ながら\" is a word used in speaking, ”つつ\" is used in writing. if you know some other similar situations regarding other words listed on JGram, please post this kind of explanation, won't you.",
      "credits_raw": "beholder",
      "content_sha256": "7942b70c0ed913942b06fb9da02afac7c3410210e7832eb072d8fe2f4d063c98",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "ながら is used in both in speaking and in writing.",
      "html": "ながら is used in both in speaking and in writing.",
      "credits_raw": "anon",
      "content_sha256": "e978148c63c7f3a5f52f9f3b2a4610385089b4d4f21aaed039dd662c5a6990d6",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "ながら can only be used when the subject of the two actions is the same; use Vte-iru aida if there are two different people doing two things at the same time. Also, the action expressed by Vm nagara is always secondary to the action expressed in the main clause.",
      "html": "ながら can only be used when the subject of the two actions is the same; use Vte-iru aida if there are two different people doing two things at the same time. Also, the action expressed by Vm nagara is always secondary to the action expressed in the main clause.",
      "credits_raw": "yookoso",
      "content_sha256": "f268ac548732be45e9ec07c33a091fd45a71ab3d489455482bc391ae168ba0b8",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Pls see also つつ",
      "html": "Pls see also つつ",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "92b9b5c81342b0eb83ae405bfdba4f86b14c9d3bbec63bfa4103fd177386a0cc",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "On a minor note, in Japanese '二人' this, that and the other is common usage while in English 'the pair' would generally sound odd - and 'They' be used in its place.",
      "html": "On a minor note, in Japanese '二人' this, that and the other is common usage while in English 'the pair' would generally sound odd - and 'They' be used in its place.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "e97caae38ec84487b4353b93ce05c6b857ce1bcddc286e3228cee7d0424c58f2",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Formed from Verb -masu base + nagara.\n\nVm = Verb -masu base",
      "html": "Formed from Verb -masu base + nagara.<br/><br/>Vm = Verb -masu base",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "442759b006a4699db598598a125514596d278d904eaddd0fbb18068f07607307",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
